# Real client IP for staging behind the VPS's shared Caddy.
#
# The path is Cloudflare -> Caddy -> nginx. nginx's TCP peer is therefore
# always Caddy, on the baja-edge Docker network (10.201.0.0/24, created by the
# Caddy stack), and never Cloudflare. So:
#
#   - The ONLY trusted proxy is baja-edge. Cloudflare's ranges are left out on
#     purpose, not forgotten: no request reaches nginx from them, and listing
#     them would only add addresses to trust for no reason.
#   - The header is still CF-Connecting-IP. Caddy passes it through unchanged,
#     so it holds what Cloudflare saw: the visitor's address.
#
# THIS IS SAFE ONLY BECAUSE CADDY ADMITS THE STAGING HOSTNAMES SOLELY FROM
# CLOUDFLARE'S IP RANGES (and answers 403 to anyone else). Trusting baja-edge
# means believing whatever CF-Connecting-IP Caddy hands over. If Caddy ever
# accepted these hostnames from any address, anybody could connect to the VPS
# directly, send their own CF-Connecting-IP, and choose the IP nginx, PHP's
# rate limiter and phpBB see. If that Caddy rule changes, change this file in
# the same breath.
#
# Not real_ip_recursive: CF-Connecting-IP holds one address, not a chain.
set_real_ip_from 10.201.0.0/24;
real_ip_header CF-Connecting-IP;
